{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFormattedSymbolID","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLFormattedSymbolIDV","text":"MXLFormattedSymbolID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldirection\/kind-swift.struct\/content-swift.enum\/symbol(_:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDirection\/Kind-swift.struct\/Content-swift.enum\/symbol(_:)"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"case","title":"MXLDirection.Kind.Content.symbol(_:)","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLDirectionV4KindV7ContentO6symbolyAgA20MXLFormattedSymbolIDVcAGmF","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLFormattedSymbolIDV","text":"MXLFormattedSymbolID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Case"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol element specifies a musical symbol using a canonical SMuFL glyph name. It is used when an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"occasional musical symbol is interspersed into text. It should not be used in place of semantic markup, such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as metronome marks that mix text and symbols. Left justification is used if not specified. Enclosure is none"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if not specified."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/docume